1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,328
[A] For the ecosystem builders out there,

2
00:00:01,328 --> 00:00:03,250
[A] I think the way that you guys do things is quite novel.

3
00:00:03,350 --> 00:00:05,150
[A] Can you speak through your process a little bit?

4
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:05,924
[A] Like how you build it,

5
00:00:05,924 --> 00:00:07,700
[A] how you're architecting this ecosystem moving forward?

6
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:10,500
[B] We take definitely a credibly neutral approach

7
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:13,300
[B] that a lot of other ecosystems disagree with.

8
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:14,778
[B] Credibly neutral doesn't mean

9
00:00:14,778 --> 00:00:17,580
[B] that we give every single team the same amount of resources

10
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:19,100
[B] because that doesn't make sense.

11
00:00:19,250 --> 00:00:20,976
[B] But what we do is we double down

12
00:00:20,976 --> 00:00:22,869
[B] on the teams that are able to show

13
00:00:22,869 --> 00:00:24,985
[B] user retention and traction themselves

14
00:00:24,985 --> 00:00:26,600
[B] because that's actually where

15
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:29,242
[B] the resources and the attention will go the furthest.

16
00:00:29,242 --> 00:00:31,648
[B] But actually making it like a level playing ground

17
00:00:31,648 --> 00:00:33,283
[B] for everyone to get to that stage,

18
00:00:33,283 --> 00:00:35,640
[B] I would say that's kind of like the core thesis.
